From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ws2_32: empty lookups, WSACleanup error, IPv6 answers on a machine without IPv6

From Wine's own protocol tests (todo_wine, recorded from Windows):
GetAddrInfoExW with neither name nor service fails at once with
WSAHOST_NOT_FOUND without starting an asynchronous lookup; a successful
WSACleanup leaves no error; and getaddrinfo leaves the IPv6 addresses of a
host name out when the machine has no IPv6 address to use (WSANO_DATA when
only IPv6 was asked for; loopback and v4-mapped addresses stay). 13
todo_wine marks removed from dlls/ws2_32/tests/protocol.c.

Gate: test/ws2ground-gate.sh (64 and 32 bit; the IPv6 rows need name
resolution and say so when they have none). Mutants SG_MUTANT_WS_NONAME,
SG_MUTANT_WS_CLEANUP and SG_MUTANT_WS_IPV6 are caught.
